<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>

<section xml:id="LabsPolicies">
    <title>Lab Policies</title>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>Purpose</title>

        <p>
            The purpose of labs is to use Google Colab/Python to explore linear
            algebra almost always through investigating important applications
            of the subject.
        </p>
    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>Instructions</title>

        <p>
            Lab activities will be more involved than class activities.
            There will be three labs this semester.
            We'll start these labs in class and you will work as a team of 2-4.
            Your final solutions should be typed up in a report and turned in
            with all of the team members' names who contributed.
            Lab due dates will be communicated on the assignment and through
            Blackboard.
        </p>

        <p>
            Your lab should have the following components:
            <ol>
                <li>Title with author names</li>
                <li>Abstract</li>
                <li>Introduction</li>
                <li>Methods and Model Description</li>
                <li>Results</li>
                <li>Discussion</li>
            </ol>
            See descriptions and further details related to these components
            <url href="https://www.reed.edu/writing/paper_help/labreport.html">at this website from Reed College</url>.
            You can use Word, LaTeX, or another document typing application to
            write up your report.
            In order to have all group members contribute, a shared site like
            <url href="https://workspace.google.com/products/docs/">Google Docs</url>
            or <url href="www.overleaf.com">Overleaf</url>.
        </p>
    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>Grading and Revisions</title>

        <p>
            Each lab will be graded out of a number of points specified on the
            document.
            There will be 3 labs.
            Your total score for this part will be the number of points you earn
            divided by the total possible.
            The labs are worth 20% of your final grade.
            At the end of the semester you'll have the opportunity to revise and
            turn in 2 labs for a better grade.
            This will be done individually.
        </p>
    </paragraphs>

    <paragraphs>
        <title>Academic Honesty</title>

        <p>
            You can work together within your group and ask your Professor for
            help.
            Using resources besides Google Colab, your classmates, and your
            Professor is not allowed.
            In particular do not google or ask ChatGPT these questions!
            All answers should be in your own words.
            Do not share electronic documents with people outside your group.
            Give yourself time and ask for help!
        </p>
    </paragraphs>
</section>